    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="0902" n="890" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg890"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.248/5–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-05T19:00:00+03:06">May 5, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 5—3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>194. ReLegs No. 192, May 5, 3 p.m.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d870-f1"/>.
                    Grafftey-Smith just informed me that he has received his instructions to support
                    the proposal <pb facs="0903" n="891" xml:id="pg891"/> for a United States
                    airfield at Dhahran and is writing to the Saudi Government to that
                        effect.<anchor n="98" xml:id="d870-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am therefore requesting permission of the King to visit him with Colonel Connor
                    May 9. Will confirm date later.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Cairo as No. 113 for Colonel Connor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d870-f1" n="97" xml:id="d870-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d870-f2" n="98" xml:id="d870-f2-content">
                <p>A copy of the British Minister’s note of May 6, 1945 to the Saudi Arabian Acting
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs was transmitted to the Department in despatch 123,
                    May 7, from Jidda (not printed).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
